   408	### 3.1 What descends, and to what
   409	
   410	Suppose `ψ(γ_∞)=1`. Then `ψ` descends to `\barψ : π_1(P²-C') ↠ S_3`; let `X` be the
   411	normalisation of `P²` in the degree-3 field extension attached to the `S_3`-action on
   412	three points. `X` is normal and irreducible (`S_3` is transitive), and `X→P²` is finite
   413	surjective, hence a **normal triple cover** (Sh12 Remark 0.2, quoted in the charged
   414	TORUS-CHECK §4.1). Over a generic point of `C'` the local monodromy is a transposition,
   415	and `\barψ` is defined on `π_1(P²-C')`, so `π` is étale outside `C'`:
