   717	   minimum possible margin.
   718	
   719	### 5.4 A structural remark for the remaining rows
   720	
   721	The reduction of Theorem A exists precisely when a triangular target shear can drop the
   722	degree, i.e. when `\deg Q \mid \deg P` (so that `φ(y)=y^{d/n}` matches the top degree).
   723	Among the residual rows:
   724	
   725	```text
   726	   (8,4):  4 | 8   → reduces to (6,4).      [this lane]
   727	   (6,4):  4 ∤ 6   → no shear reduction.    [killed by TORUS-CHECK on its own geometry]
   728	   (8,6):  6 ∤ 8   → no shear reduction.
   729	   (9,6):  6 ∤ 9   → no shear reduction.
   730	```
   731	
   732	So rows `(8,6)` and `(9,6)` are **not** reachable by this argument and genuinely need
   733	either their own `§1`-style geometry or the nodal-realisation obstruction already typed
   734	in ROW-SWEEP §§7, 9. Nothing here bears on them, nor on
   735	`OPEN[NA-R1-SHARPNESS-IRREDUCIBLE]`, `OPEN[NORI-BC-SELF-TANGENT-COEFF]`, or
   736	`OPEN[PI1S4-D1-DEGREE]`.
