   439	closure of `γ_∞`, so `ψ` descends to a surjection `ψ̄ : π₁(P²−F̄_j) ↠ S_3`. Let
   440	`X` be the normalisation of `P²` in the degree-3 field extension attached to the
   441	`S_3`-action on 3 points; `X` is normal, irreducible (`S_3` is transitive), and
   442	`X → P²` is finite surjective, hence a normal triple cover (Sh12 Rem 0.2).
   443	
   444	Its branch divisor: over a generic point of `F̄_j` the local monodromy is a transposition,
   445	so `F̄_j ⊆ S_π` with index 2 and multiplicity 1 in `Δ_π`. Nothing else is in the branch
   446	locus: `ψ̄` is defined on `π₁(P²−F̄_j)`, so `X → P²` is étale over `P² ∖ F̄_j`. Hence
   447	
   448	```text
   449	   S_π = F̄_j ,   T_π = 0 ,   Δ_π = F̄_j ,   deg Δ_π = 6 .
   450	```
   451	
   452	Corollary 0.6 now applies and its "only if" direction gives condition (1): `F̄_j` is
