   474	## 5. The affine bridge: escape (a) — branching along `L_∞`
   475	
   476	This is the new work. The campaign's `φ` lives on `C²−D_j`; the theorems of §4 live on
   477	`P²`. The gap is one element: `ψ(γ_∞)`, the image of the meridian of the line at
   478	infinity. I compute it exactly, with no braid-monodromy data.
   479	
   480	### 5.1 What is a priori available
   481	
   482	`H_1(C²−D_j) = Z⟨g⟩` (`D_j` irreducible), and `γ_∞ = 6g` there (a generic line meets
   483	`D_j` in 6 points). The sign character `S_3 → Z/2` kills `γ_∞` because `6` is even, so
   484	
   485	```text
   486	   ψ(γ_∞) ∈ A_3 ≅ Z/3   —   and, S_4-side,  φ(γ_∞) ∈ A_4 .                    (5.1)
   487	```
