   530	of `D̄_j` on `L_∞` is `Q_∞ = [1:0:0] ≠ Q'`. Hence the large circle is a genuine meridian
   531	of `L_∞` in `P² ∖ (F̄_j ∪ L_∞)`:
   532	
   533	```text
   534	   γ_∞ = g_6 g_5 g_4 g_3 g_2 g_1     (in the adapted geometric basis).           (5.4)
   535	```
