+then (2.1) descends to (\pi_1(\mathbb P^2-\bar D)).  Normalizing
+(\mathbb P^2) in the associated index-five field gives a connected normal finite
+map (f:X\to\mathbb P^2) of degree five, unramified off (\bar D), with generic
+inertia a transposition.  There is no divisorial ramification on (L_\infty).
