   110	through this one-curve complement (`B0:550-569`; `REV:64-66,146-152`).
   111	Transitivity comes from connectedness of the five-sheeted cover, and a transitive
   112	group generated by transpositions is (S_5): its transpositions are edges of a
   113	connected graph on five vertices.  At every self-double point the two branch
   114	meridians are **disjoint** transpositions.  Equal transpositions fix three letters,
   115	and transpositions sharing one letter fix two, whereas the reviewed local fibre has
   116	one fixed letter.  The incidence correction in §1 merely changes where that fixed
   117	letter is represented; it does not alter this conclusion.
