   122	normal subgroup meeting (A_5) trivially would inject into (S_5/A_5); a nontrivial
   123	order-two normal subgroup would then be central, contrary to (Z(S_5)=1).  Therefore
   124	
   125	\[
   126	                         S_5/A_5\simeq C_2                         \tag{2.2}
   127	\]
   128	
   129	is the only nontrivial proper quotient.  There is no (S_5\twoheadrightarrow S_3),
   130	and no analogue of (S_4\twoheadrightarrow S_4/V_4\simeq S_3).  In particular,
   131	the N=4 chain “transpositions to transpositions in a triple cover to normal-triple-
   132	plane classification” stops at its first arrow.
