   134	There are useful *permutation resolvents*, but they are not quotients:
   135	
   136	| action | degree | image of a natural transposition | consequence |
   137	|---|---:|---|---|
   138	| natural (S_5/S_4) | 5 | (1^3 2) | the original quintic cover |
   139	| sign (S_5/A_5) | 2 | (2) | double cover; loses the (A_5) layer |
   140	| six Sylow-5 subgroups | 6 | (2^3) | classical sextic resolvent, faithful |
   141	| two-element subsets | 10 | (1^4 2^3) | faithful degree-ten resolvent |
   142	
   143	For the degree-six line, a stabilizer is the order-20 normalizer of a 5-cycle.
   144	A transposition normalizes no Sylow-5 subgroup (the involutions in that affine
   145	normalizer have natural type (1 2^2)), hence has no fixed point and type (2^3).
   146	For the degree-ten line, ({1,2}) and the three pairs disjoint from it are fixed,
   147	while ({1,j}) and ({2,j}) are swapped for (j=3,4,5).  Neither action produces a
   148	simply branched triple cover.  Calling either one “the (S_5) quotient” would
   149	confuse an associated cover with a normal quotient.
   150	
   151	The sign factor is exact but weak.  It makes the Galois closure factor through the
   152	double plane fixed by (A_5); the remaining layer has group (A_5).  For even (d),
   153	sign already kills the infinity meridian, but an even permutation can still be a
   154	nontrivial value of (\rho(\gamma_\infty)).  Thus sign-triviality must not be
   155	substituted for full INF-TRIVIAL.
   156	
   157	### 2.2 What full INF-TRIVIAL would give
   158	
   159	Let (\gamma_\infty) be a meridian of (L_\infty) in the affine complement.  If
   160	
   161	\[
   162	                         \rho(\gamma_\infty)=1,                    \tag{2.3}
   163	\]
   164	
   165	then (2.1) descends to (\pi_1(\mathbb P^2-\bar D)).  Normalizing
   166	(\mathbb P^2) in the associated index-five field gives a connected normal finite
   167	map (f:X\to\mathbb P^2) of degree five, unramified off (\bar D), with generic
   168	inertia a transposition.  There is no divisorial ramification on (L_\infty).
   169	Because a normal surface is Cohen--Macaulay and the base is regular of dimension
   170	two, this finite map is flat.  Writing
   171	(f_*\mathcal O_X=\mathcal O\oplus E^\vee), (\operatorname{rk}E=4), its trace
   172	discriminant gives
   173	
   174	\[
   175	                  \mathcal O_{\mathbb P^2}(\bar D)\simeq(\det E)^2. \tag{2.4}
