+\[
+                             \Pi^n=1.                              \tag{5.1}
+\]
+
+Extend the entries periodically as in the standard Theorem A proof.  Coprimality
+of $d,n$ makes all entries one orbit under conjugation by $\Pi$.  Such an orbit
+of transpositions generates $S_5$ exactly when its edge orbit is connected on
+five vertices.  Enumerating the seven cycle types in $S_5$ leaves only
+
+| cycle type of $\Pi$ | connected edge orbit | forced arithmetic |
+|---|---|---|
+| $(3)(2)$ | all six edges of $K_{3,2}$ | $6\mid n$, $d$ odd |
+| $(4)(1)$ | the four-edge star from the fixed letter | $4\mid n$, $d$ odd |
+| $(5)$ | a five-cycle (or its diagonal cycle) | $5\mid n$, $d$ even |
